# Realtime Socket.IO Safety

- Treat every socket event payload as untrusted input.
- Keep event names and payload fields stable and documented.
- Avoid long blocking work inside socket handlers.
- Emit server events only after successful state transitions.
- Handle disconnect/reconnect paths explicitly.
- Add at least one test or reproducible scenario for critical socket changes.
